       text-transform: uppercase;
     }

     h1 {
       margin: 0;
       font-size: clamp(2rem, 3vw, 3rem);
       line-height: 1.1;
     }

     .intro {
       margin: 14px 0 0;
       max-width: 62ch;
       color: var(--muted);
       font-size: 1rem;
       line-height: 1.6;
     }

     .faq-list {
       margin-top: 28px;
       display: grid;
       gap: 14px;
     }

     .example {
       border: 1px solid rgba(125, 211, 252, 0.14);
       border-radius: 18px;
       background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.9);
       overflow: hidden;
       transition: border-color 0.2s ease, transform 0.2s ease, box-shadow 0.2s ease;
     }

     .example:hover,
     .example:focus-within {
       border-color: rgba(125, 211, 252, 0.4);
       transform: translateY(-1px);
       box-shadow: 0 14px 30px rgba(8, 15, 30, 0.28);
     }

     .question {
       width: 100%;
       border: 0;
       background: transparent;
       color: inherit;
       display: flex;
       align-items: center;
       justify-content: space-between;
       gap: 16px;
       padding: 20px 22px;
       text-align: left;
       font: inherit;
       font-size: 1.05rem;
       font-weight: 700;
       cursor: pointer;
     }

     .question:focus-visible {
       outline: 3px solid rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.55);
       outline-offset: -3px;
     }

     .icon {
       flex: 0 0 auto;
       width: 2rem;
       height: 2rem;
       border-radius: 999px;
       display: inline-grid;
       place-items: center;
       background: rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.12);
       color: var(--accent);
       font-size: 1.3rem;
       transition: transform 0.2s ease, background-color 0.2s ease;
     }

     .question[aria-expanded="true"] .icon {
       transform: rotate(45deg);
       background: rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.2);
     }

     .details {
       padding: 0 22px 20px;
       color: var(--muted);
       line-height: 1.7;
     }

     .details p {
       margin: 0;
     }

     .details[hidden] {
       display: none;
     }

     @media (max-width: 640px) {
       .page {
         padding: 24px 18px;
       }

       .question,
       .details {
         padding-left: 18px;
         padding-right: 18px;
       }
     }
   </style>
 </head>
 <body>
   <main class="page">
     <p class="eyebrow">Cat Care Guide</p>
     <h1>Frequently asked questions about cats</h1>
     <p class="intro">
       Learn the basics of feline behavior, health, and daily care with quick answers designed for curious cat owners.
     </p>

     <section class="faq-list" aria-label="Cat frequently asked questions">
       <div class="example">
         <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-1">
           Why do cats purr?
           <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
         </button>
         <div class="details" id="faq-1" hidden>
           <p>Cats often purr when they feel relaxed and safe, but they may also purr to comfort themselves when stressed, injured, or recovering. The sound is usually a sign of emotion, not just happiness.</p>
         </div>
       </div>

       <div class="example">
         <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-2">
           How much sleep do cats need?
           <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
         </button>
         <div class="details" id="faq-2" hidden>
           <p>Most adult cats sleep between 12 and 16 hours a day. Kittens and senior cats may rest even longer because growth and aging both increase the need for recovery time.</p>
         </div>
       </div>

       <div class="example">
         <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-3">
           Why do cats knead with their paws?
           <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
         </button>
         <div class="details" id="faq-3" hidden>
           <p>Kneading starts in kittenhood during nursing and often stays as a soothing habit in adulthood. Cats may knead when they feel content, when they are making a resting spot, or when they want attention.</p>
         </div>
       </div>

       <div class="example">
         <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-4">
           What should cats eat?
           <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
         </button>
         <div class="details" id="faq-4" hidden>
           <p>Cats are obligate carnivores, so they need a complete diet rich in animal-based protein and nutrients such as taurine. A balanced commercial cat food made for their age and health needs is usually the safest choice.</p>
         </div>
       </div>

       <div class="example">
         <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-5">
           Why do cats scratch furniture?
           <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
         </button>
         <div class="details" id="faq-5" hidden>
           <p>Scratching helps cats stretch, mark territory, and maintain their claws. Offering sturdy scratching posts near favorite resting spots can redirect the behavior without trying to stop the natural instinct.</p>
         </div>
       </div>

       <div class="example">
         <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-6">
           How can I help a cat feel comfortable at home?
           <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
         </button>
         <div class="details" id="faq-6" hidden>
           <p>Create a calm routine with fresh water, clean litter, quiet hiding places, vertical climbing space, and daily play. Cats usually settle in faster when they can observe their surroundings and approach people on their own terms.</p>
         </div>
       </div>
     </section>
   </main>

   <script>
     const questions = document.querySelectorAll(".question");

     questions.forEach((button) => {
       button.addEventListener("click", () => {
         const details = document.getElementById(button.getAttribute("aria-controls"));
         const isExpanded = button.getAttribute("aria-expanded") === "true";

         button.setAttribute("aria-expanded", String(!isExpanded));
         details.hidden = isExpanded;
       });
     });
   </script>
 </body>
 </html>

')
